<CREATED>1795653276</CREATED>
<DESC><![CDATA[The Security Council,

Understanding the noble goal of recognizing the biggest and the largest creatures as important parts of the ecosystems that they inhabit,

Noting the affront to this that is SC#361 which noble in its goal in trying to recognize this mission fails utterly and totally at these aims,

Recognizing the blatant falsehood of the second clause in its recognition due to the existence in the multiverse of the Pygmy hippopotamus and other smaller varieties of these creatures,

Questioning why hippopotamuses are noted as being large themselves when bigger larger creatures exist such as the noble and much larger blue whale,

Believing that just because a creature is large that it does not warrant its own resolution on the topic serving nothing but to mock larger creatures,

Hereby repeals &#147;Declaration on Hippopotamuses&#148;.]]></DESC>
